# A shell script has to reach a Linux runner with LF endings: CRLF turns the
# shebang into `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, and the runner answers `bad interpreter`.
# A Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true converts on checkout, so the working
# copy is where this goes wrong even when the index is clean.
#
# This repository has no line-ending policy otherwise and this file does not
# introduce one. It pins the one file type where the ending is executable
# semantics rather than style; everything else keeps whatever it has today.
*.sh text eol=lf
